CAVEAT:  Proven with one ingress interface, one far subnet, two forwarded UDP ports
         (69 and 37) and one unhelped control port (7777), at 5 frames per flow.
         No real UDP service answered: the far side is a capture, so what is proven
         is what the DUT relays, not what a server behind it does with it. The
         relay was not exercised across more than one hop, against a helper address
         that is not directly connected, or with the ingress interface in a VRF
         (there is no VRF form of the command -- see STEP 0).

