  => STEP 4 PASS: both of the guide's remaining sentences hold, and the difference
     is visible in the ETHERNET header rather than only the IP header. Multiple
     `ip helper-address` lines on one interface each get their own copy: 10 helped
     broadcasts went in and 20 relayed frames came out, two per ingress frame. And
     the helper address that is the broadcast address of a directly connected
     subnet was forwarded as a TRUE link-layer broadcast onto that subnet, in the
     same capture as a unicast copy to an ordinary host address -- two different
     treatments produced from one ingress frame by one feature. The 7777 control
     was still relayed 0 times.

